From: Harvi654 <202698022+Harvi654@users.noreply.github.com>
Subject: mshtml: Accept an omitted document open result.

AI-assisted (Codex), original code; LGPL-2.1-or-later. Not submitted upstream.

Our own Windows 10 x86_64/i686 MEASURE opens fresh, initialized and loaded
HTML documents successfully with either a supplied result pointer or NULL.
A supplied pointer receives a non-NULL dispatch, but callers may omit it.
Wine unconditionally writes through the pointer before checking the document
and again when returning the successful window result. Guard both writes
and acquire the output reference only when a result was requested.

v2 (2026-11-09): Keep the production guards unchanged and add a Wine test
beside the existing document open tests. Use fresh copies of our loaded,
ready HTML for the positive control and NULL case, checking the measured
S_OK and usable parent window before and after close. Do not assert a
returned dispatch interface type unrelated to this fix. These assertions
still need native L1 and paired Wine runtime validation. Unpatched Wine
faults at the unconditional NULL output write; do not skip that call or
turn the fault into an expected Windows result. No production series change.

